      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Maybe also have thread_local 'defaults for these control settings.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Maybe ONLY the thread_local stuff is helpful.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "BUt could also use the new feature of ToString () - that it a takes ... template parameterpack - last arg - so extra values passed trhoguh.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "—",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "\t Consider using perfect forwarding on Characters::ToString () to allow passing extra args, and then for floats, allow optionally passing the numerical formatting properites I’ve defined in Stroika (precsion)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "type" : "rule"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "\tSimilarly for integers – saying – maybe – the format string? – for hex/nohex? – no – format string not safe – but flag saying hex/nohex is safe – maybe like we have flaoatingformatting file – have integerformatting file?",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "type" : "rule"
            }
         ],
